From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: keep SDI enabled for ramdump testing

qcom_scm disables the firmware's watchdog debug/SDI at probe unless
download mode was requested on the command line, so a dump armed later
at runtime has no CPU contexts. Leave SDI as the firmware set it
(module parameter keep_sdi, default on) for s2idle hang ramdumps.
Test only; drop before merging.
---
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -38,6 +38,10 @@
 
 static u32 download_mode;
 
+/* Ramdump testing: keep the firmware watchdog CPU-context dump (SDI) enabled */
+static bool keep_sdi = true;
+module_param(keep_sdi, bool, 0444);
+
 #define GIC_SPI_BASE        32
 #define GIC_MAX_SPI       1019  // SPIs in GICv3 spec range from 32..1019
 #define GIC_ESPI_BASE     4096
@@ -2849,7 +2853,9 @@ static int qcom_scm_probe(struct platfor
 	/*
 	 * Disable SDI if indicated by DT that it is enabled by default.
 	 */
-	if (of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "qcom,sdi-enabled") || !download_mode)
+	if (keep_sdi)
+		dev_info(scm->dev, "leaving SDI enabled\n");
+	else if (of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "qcom,sdi-enabled") || !download_mode)
 		qcom_scm_disable_sdi();
 
 	/*
